# Icebergs show one tranche at a time; the rest stays hidden. Each new tranche joins the back of the queue, so the
# hidden part never jumps ahead of orders that were displayed first.
> add ACME
added ACME
> sell 300 @ 100.00 display=100
ACME #1 SELL 300 @ 100.00 display 100 -> resting 300
> sell 50 @ 100.00
ACME #2 SELL 50 @ 100.00 -> resting 50
> book
ACME  CONTINUOUS  last -  resting 2
              BID                       ASK
                               100.00 x 150     (2)
> order 1
ACME #1 SELL 300 @ 100.00 GTC, sequence 1, iceberg showing 100 (tranches of 100)

# The buy fills the visible tranche of order 1. Its next tranche goes behind order 2, which fills next.
> buy 120 @ 100.00
ACME #3 BUY 120 @ 100.00 -> filled 120
  trade #1  100 @ 100.00  buy #3  sell #1
  trade #2  20 @ 100.00  buy #3  sell #2
> book
ACME  CONTINUOUS  last 100.00  resting 2
              BID                       ASK
                               100.00 x 130     (2)
> order 1
ACME #1 SELL 200 @ 100.00 GTC, sequence 4, iceberg showing 100 (tranches of 100)

# Order 2's last 30, then order 1's last two tranches. The unfilled 20 rests.
> buy 250 @ 100.00
ACME #4 BUY 250 @ 100.00 -> filled 230, resting 20
  trade #3  30 @ 100.00  buy #4  sell #2
  trade #4  100 @ 100.00  buy #4  sell #1
  trade #5  100 @ 100.00  buy #4  sell #1
> book
ACME  CONTINUOUS  last 100.00  resting 1
              BID                       ASK
     100.00 x 20      (1)
